## <%if .DisplayName%><%.DisplayName%><%else%><%.Slug%><%end%> — shape: fan-out reviewers + deterministic convergence.
##
## A router runs two read-only reviewers in parallel, each with its own
## lens on the same diff; a compute (`await: wait_all`) folds their
## verdicts without an LLM; a typed failure carries a blocked verdict.
## Fill in: the lenses, the scope (`git diff HEAD` or a base ref). A
## third reviewer is one more node and two more edges. docs/routers.md
<%template "vars_block" .%>
schema findings:
  findings: string[]
  blocking: bool

schema verdict_out:
  approved: bool

prompt mission:
<%indent 2 .Instructions%>

prompt correctness_lens:
  Lens: CORRECTNESS. Run `git add -N . && git diff HEAD` (or diff against
  {{vars.base}} when it is set) and hunt for real bugs: logic errors,
  missed edge cases, races. Read enough surrounding code to judge each
  finding. Report each confirmed finding as file:line plus the failure
  scenario, and set blocking=true if any must be fixed before merge.
  Do not edit any file.

prompt security_lens:
  Lens: SECURITY. Same diff: look for injection, unsafe deserialisation,
  secrets in code, missing authorisation checks, SSRF. Same report shape,
  same rule on blocking, no edits.

router split:
  mode: fan_out_all

agent review_correctness:<%template "llm_fields" .%>
  system: mission
  user: correctness_lens
  readonly: true
  output: findings

agent review_security:<%template "llm_fields" .%>
  system: mission
  user: security_lens
  readonly: true
  output: findings

## Deterministic convergence: no LLM decides whether the reviews block.
compute verdict:
  await: wait_all
  output: verdict_out
  expr:
    approved: "!outputs.review_correctness.blocking && !outputs.review_security.blocking"

fail review_blocked:
  description: "a reviewer found a blocking issue"
  code: REVIEW_BLOCKED
  message: "blocking: correctness={{outputs.review_correctness.blocking}} security={{outputs.review_security.blocking}}"

workflow <%.WorkflowName%>:
  entry: split
  budget:
    max_parallel_branches: 2<%template "budget_lines" .%><%template "worktree_dial" .%><%template "dials" .%>
  split -> review_correctness
  split -> review_security
  review_correctness -> verdict
  review_security -> verdict
  verdict -> done when approved
  verdict -> review_blocked else
